  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "改變世界的科學知識",
    "sub_ename": "INTERPRETING LIFE IN LITERATURE",
    "describe_ch": "本課程從科學技術的知識原理出發，解析諾貝爾獎(包含物理、化學、醫學、經濟學…等)對人類生活產生的重大改變，用人文反思和討論、實作的方式，讓學生掌握科學技術的原始核心概念，關注日常生活中科學原理如何體現，進而促使學生充分瞭解科學發展和生活的相關性，將科技發展融入社會經濟發展活動之中，並思考如何應對真實問題，以及人類未來如何永續發展等議題。",
    "describe_eh": "This course begins from the knowledge principles of science and technology, analyzes the major changes of the Nobel Prize (including physics, chemistry, medicine, economics, etc.) on human life.\nThroughout the course, humanistic reflection, discussion and practical work are used to enable students to grasp the original core concepts of science and technology, and to pay attention to how principles of science are embodied in our daily life, which in turn leads to a full understanding of the relevance of scientific development and life.",
    "pre_subname": "",
    "pre_sub_id3": null,
    "pre_sub_ename": "",
    "pre_describe": null,
    "pre_describe_en": null,
    "scr_credit": 2.0
  },
